<figure class="wp-block-table alignwide is-style-discrepancy"><table><thead><tr><th>Detail</th><th>Mark</th><th>Matthew</th><th>Luke</th><th>John</th><th>Thomas</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Where it appears</td><td><code>14:12-26</code></td><td><code>26:17-30</code></td><td><code>22:7-39</code></td><td><code>13:1-17:26</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Relation to Passover</td><td>A Passover meal on the first day of Unleavened Bread <code>14:12</code></td><td>A Passover meal <code>26:17-19</code></td><td>“I have eagerly desired to eat this Passover with you” <code>22:15</code></td><td>“Before the Feast of the Passover” <code>13:1</code>; the next day the leaders avoid entering the governor’s house to keep the Passover <code>18:28</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Foot washing</td><td>None</td><td>None</td><td>None</td><td>Jesus washes the disciples’ feet <code>13:1-17</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Bread and cup</td><td>Bread, then cup <code>14:22-24</code></td><td>Bread, then cup <code>26:26-28</code></td><td>Cup, bread, then cup in the longer text <code>22:17-20</code></td><td>None</td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>“For the forgiveness of sins”</td><td>Not said</td><td>Said over the cup <code>26:28</code></td><td>Not said</td><td>Not said</td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Betrayer named</td><td>Not named; “one who is eating with me” <code>14:18-20</code></td><td>Judas answers “Is it I?” and is told “You have said so” <code>26:25</code></td><td>Not named; the betrayer’s hand is on the table <code>22:21</code></td><td>Judas, to whom Jesus gives the dipped morsel <code>13:26</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Denial of Peter foretold</td><td>On the way to the Mount of Olives <code>14:26-31</code></td><td>On the way to the Mount of Olives <code>26:30-35</code></td><td>At the supper <code>22:31-34</code></td><td>At the supper <code>13:36-38</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>After the meal</td><td>The Mount of Olives and Gethsemane <code>14:26,32</code></td><td>The Mount of Olives and Gethsemane <code>26:30,36</code></td><td>The Mount of Olives <code>22:39</code></td><td>A long discourse, then a garden across the Kidron <code>14:1-18:1</code></td><td>No account</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<!-- /wp:table -->
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The first three gospels place the arrest after a Passover meal; John places the supper before Passover and gives no words over bread and cup. Thomas has no account of a last meal, and no saying makes bread or a cup the body or blood of Jesus.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
